  "oraclefix2": "2026-10-05: orient_for_handoff tilts at 0.02 s per 0.5 deg sample and holds 1 s (was 0.05 s and 8 s). Under the Harbor instance's 2.5 ms x 10 physics the slower tilt lets the ring slide 43 mm along the lower band into the right gripper, where it wedges between the fingers and the active pickup lifts the remainder with it (lab oraclefix2/exp/X1h, X4); after the fast tilt the released ring hangs free of the puzzle (separating gap +36 mm, X3e), the left hand grasps it, the right hand withdraws out of it and the ring is placed (native success at 297.2 s sim, X10, with the query-budgeted free-arm transits).",
  "mujoco_changes": "2026-10-10, MuJoCo port: grasp_ring's release_translation_m [0, 0.22, 0] -> [0.05, 0.14, 0] (the left arm's reach). 2026-10-11: that reference was judged VIOLENT by the stress observer: the right hand opened 0.15-0.4 m above the table and the dropped remainder spun a chain link at 92 rad/s; lowering both hands first was measured and does not give a fall that is both CLEAN and on the system side (docs/rcb/families/horseshoe_ring.md). 2026-10-11, on the soft contact class at a constant impedance: the hand-off after the support release is a hand swap instead (support_release hand_swap, step drop_ring_by_hand_swap; swap.py): after the upper shoe is let go the ring hangs on the right hand's two fingers, free of the puzzle; the left hand takes the lower shoe by its other leg, the right hand opens (the weld passes to the left hand), the left hand moves the remainder 4 cm further onto the system side and the right hand carries the ring on its open fingers over the goal region. The task's goal (ring inside the region and quiet, remainder on the system side, holding allowed) is met there, with the remainder still in the left hand. Nothing is dropped. grasp_ring / place_ring (the active pickup) are no longer steps. The task, its separator and its success rule are unchanged."
